t\t\t Materials Breakdown Timeline (PDF) \r\n\t\t\t\t Transfer Station Guidelines \r\n\t\t\t\t Transfer Station Prices (PDF) \r\n\t\t\t\t Battery Disposal \r\n\t\t\t Water & Wastewater Department \r\n\t\t\t\t Clean Drinking Water Is up to You (PDF) \r\n\t\t\t\t Consumer Confidence Reports \r\n\t\t\t\t Forms & Applications \r\n\t\t\t\t Groundwater Protection Letter to Residents (PDF) \r\n\t\t\t\t Sewer Use Ordinance (PDF) \r\n\t\t\t\t Water Quality Reports \r\n\t\t\t\t Water Rules and Regulations (PDF) \r\n\t\t\t\t Best Management Practices (BMPs) for Groundwater Protection \r\n\t\t\t Welfare Department \r\n\t\t\t\t Applications & Required Forms \r\n\t\t\t\t Town Guidelines (PDF) \r\nHome \nDepartments \r\nDepartments\t\t \r\n9 \n1 \n1 \n2 \t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t Administration \r\nAdministration page outlines the leadership and operational structure of Farmington’s town government \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Assessing \r\nAssessing page provides information and reports from the Assessing Office, detailing property assessments, tax data, and contact information for the assessing staff. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Economic Development \r\nView the info about Farmington Economic Development (committee, documents, revitalization zone) on this page. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Farmington Area Schools \r\nVisit the Farmington Area Schools on this page. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Farmington Community Television \r\nFarmington Community TV streams and archives public town and committee meetings with a broadcast schedule and contact info. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Farmington Fire & Rescue \r\nFarmington Fire Rescue provides 24-hour fire and EMS service for about 7,000 residents over 37.5 square miles. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Farmington Senior Center \r\nThe Farmington Senior Center page provides information about staff contacts. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Parks & Recreation Department \r\nFarmington Parks and Recreation Department offers summer camps after school programs special events and maintains parks and facilities. It also supports senior and outdoor activities. Hours are 9 AM to 5:30 PM weekdays. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Planning & Community Development \r\nThe Planning and Community Development Department handles building permits code enforcement zoning land use planning and public complaint processes. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Police Department \r\nVisit Farmington NH Police Department on this page. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Public Works Department \r\nThe Public Works Department page outlines the department’s mission, office hours, contact information, and staff contacts, highlighting services that support Farmington’s infrastructure. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Town Administrator \r\nThe Town Administrator page introduces Ken Dickie. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Town Clerk / Tax Collector \r\nTown Clerk / Tax Collector page provides office hours, election results, online payment portals, absentee ballot requests, and staff contact information. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Town Moderator \r\nAccess the Town Moderator's staff contact on this page. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Transfer Station \r\nThe Transfer Station page provides information on Farmington’s pay-as-you-throw waste program, recycling guidelines, disposal rules, and contact details for the facility supervisor. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Water & Wastewater Department \r\nWater and Wastewater Department page provides information on Farmington’s water supply system, wastewater treatment facility, service rates, and backflow testing services. \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Welfare Department \r\nThe Welfare Department page provides information on applying for assistance in Farmington, appointment scheduling, eligibility requirements, and a list of nearby homeless shelters. \r\n\t\t\t FAQs \r\n\t\t\t Minutes & Agendas \r\n\t\t\t Online Dog, Motor Vehicle, & Vital Records \r\n\t\t\t Online Tax and Water/Sewer Payment \r\n\t\t\t Building Permits \r\n\t\t\t Tax Assessments \r\nTown of Farmington \r\nFarmington Municipal Offices \r\n356 Main Street \r\nFarmington, NH 03835 \r\n         Home \n         Site Map \n         Accessibility \n         Copyright Notices \n     